       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum labeled daily dose. It has no established indication, and it carries a serious risk of GI hemorrhage, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** The options are 800 mg PO TID (2,400 mg/day), 600 mg PO QID (2,400 mg/day), or 400 mg PO QID (1,600 mg/day). A single dose of 800 mg is the usual ceiling.\n- **Enter 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day).** This is the absolute maximum, and I'd add a note like \"max daily dose, reassess need and renal function daily.\"\n- **Help you reach other options.** If the goal is more pain control, I can enter a scheduled acetaminophen order to go with the ibuprofen. If there's a specific clinical reason for this dose, talk it through with your attending or the clinical pharmacist before it's ordered.\n\nIf you tell me which option you want, I'll enter it now."
